  "body": "## What are you trying to do\n\nSelect an AGIECUT Classic 2S in the machine library and start a wire EDM setup with the manufacturer's stated capabilities. The library currently has no entry for this machine.\n\n## How you imagine it working\n\nAdd a machine template from the manufacturer's public technical handbook. Register it in the machine picker. Include the documented axis names, rapid speeds, symmetric U/V stroke and standard wire sizes. The handbook gives X/Y/Z stroke lengths. It does not supply a work zero for these strokes.\n\nLeave the installed datum, guide planes, generator conditions and post codes for the operator to supply. State clearly that the template has no native post. The native job writer is separate work in #2945.\n\nSource: [AGIE, AGIECUT Classic, edition 06.2002 C2.1, sections 1.1 and 5.2](https://static.gindumac.com/products/9ccc9b7e-b589-49db-9843-eff1da09434c/documents/ES-EDM-AGI-2002-00001.pdf).\n\nDone means: A normal library selection mounts the machine as wire EDM. Tests pin the sourced limits and verify that missing installation data stays unset. An unconfigured template must refuse a wire job.\n",
